 `POST /loops/{id}/publish` publishes whatever draft the server holds when it admits the request and returns that immutable version. The editor therefore reports what was stored, and keeps it apart from the draft it saved for the attempt and from later work in the editor.
 
-- **One attempt.** Publish refuses held input, saves, and then queues the request with the loop's saves in this window, so this editor's own later saves reach the server after it. It records the server's copy for the attempt as the save's answer (`draft.definition` and `draftToken`), or the loaded copy parsed as the server stored it when this load made no save. The queued request rechecks that the same editor load is still open and that no held input, draft conflict or name refusal appeared, and sends nothing otherwise. A second click while an attempt runs is ignored. An outcome shows only in the editor load that made it; a reply that arrives after a reload or in another editor shows nothing there.
